# UX and A2UI
- Stable Documents, Study, Reports tabs. Don't let the model replace navigation, security/account controls or document upload/delete UI.
- Dynamic A2UI may only compose schema-validated allowlisted components from authorized pinned analysis/Study data; never execute model HTML/JS, SQL or arbitrary tool actions.
- Every material case claim links to trusted fact/derived IDs and source chip; chip opens correct original physical page subject to authorization.
- Brand: user-provided unchanged PDF is the authority, and `prototype/HiveForYou V4 Prototype.dc.html` (with `prototype/assets/`) is the authoritative visual and interaction reference (D-036; `prototype/_ds/` is unused). Blue=needs you/action; Coral=missing; Honey=changed and source chip; Leaf=checked. Calm exact tone; never invent urgency or verdicts.
- Responsive accessible keyboard focus, labelled statuses, source sheet and accessible chart/table equivalents. Safe static fallback when dynamic view is invalid.
- No generated or synthetic prototype data (`prototype/hive-data.js`, `prototype/support.js`) used in `apps/web/` runtime, permissions or source-of-truth. Refer to `docs/HiveForYou-FEATURES.md` and `docs/HiveForYou-UX-A2UI-DESIGN.md`.
